    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that. but if the consensus is so solid, shouldn't the \"legitimate\" part of the debate just be about how to implement policies without being too heavy handed? it feels like when people try to frame it as a \"debate\" between science and non-science, it's kind of deceptive. like, isn't it more accurate to say it's just a conflict between public health facts and people who are wrong?",
