      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Many experts agree that the truly \"legitimate\" policy debate centers on the *method* of implementation, such as waivers or exemptions, rather than the efficacy of the science itself. Framing it solely as a conflict between facts and error risks dismissing the genuine anxieties people hold about medical intervention. Therefore, the conflict is often better understood as a friction point between established public health mandates and deeply held individual beliefs.",
